# How we work

You prompt and decide product behavior. The agent writes code. Precedence: chat instructions win over rules and docs.

## 1. Boundaries & Fixtures
- **Test pN:** Agent **never** opens, unlocks, or uploads `.local/test-pn/`. Never commit `.local/`, log passcodes/pn names, or paste secrets. No third fixture.
- **Tools off by default:** No browser MCP (`cursor-ide-browser`), Playwright, `ux-*.mjs`, `test:e2e*`, WebSearch, Task, or subagents unless explicitly requested in this chat.
- **Search scope:** Confine all searches (grep, file find) strictly to the `apps/<name>/` or `packages/<name>/` mentioned in the prompt. No monorepo-wide searches unless user explicitly says "search repo-wide" or "search entire repo". Stop reading once target component is found; do not explore sibling pages (Inbox, Settings, Search, etc.) unless asked. No stale-doc reads (`docs/archive/**`, plans, logs).

## 2. Root Cause Before Edits
- Name the user-visible symptom, trace to the external system (Drive, API, Redis, Postgres, device), and find the exact failing function.
- Fix on the path in `packages/` (apps stay thin). Delete the broken dual/shim; do not patch symptoms or leave dead paths.

## 3. Targeted Verification
- Run the touched area's unit test ONCE (never full suite / deploy preflights). Do NOT run full builds (`npm run build`, `vite build`), git status/log checks, or global typechecks (`tsc --noEmit`) unless explicitly instructed:
  - `apps/aggregator-browser/`: `npm run test:browser:unit`
  - `apps/id-dashboard/`: `npm run test:dashboard:unit`
  - `apps/pen/`: `npm run test:pen`
  - `apps/prism/`: `npm run test:prism`
  - `api/`: `npm run test:api`
  - `packages/<name>/`: `cd packages/<name> && npm test`
- Workflow tests land next to new workflows. User confirms visible UI on their own pN.

## 4. Done & Ship
- Once the single targeted test passes: `git add` the changed files for this task (no `.env`, secrets, `.local/`, `.firebase` cache) → `git commit` with why → `git push`, unless this chat explicitly says not to commit or push.
- Then output a short summary of changes and stop. Do NOT run follow-up git diffs, redundant verification loops, or full-suite tests.
- Do **not** run `./deploy.sh`, `firebase deploy`, or API deploy unless explicitly asked. Remind user once: live hosting updates when they run `./deploy.sh` from repo root.
